  ('search-cur-trainer-seven-step-method', 'cur-trainer-seven-step-method', 'module', 'The Seven-Step Training Method', 'Explain it. Show it. Rehearse it. Use it. Coach it. Prove it. Recheck it.
Outcomes: Use Teach > Demonstrate > Rehearse > Run Live > Coach > Certify > Audit; Make critical decisions visible; Separate attendance from evidence
The method: Teach: explain the purpose, observable standard, approved source, steps, decisions, and stop points.; Demonstrate: perform at normal speed, repeat with slow decision narration, then perform at normal speed again.; Rehearse: create controlled reps away from guest risk; coach one priority and rerun immediately.; Run Live: name the independence level and intervention boundary before the rep.; Coach: use observation, standard, impact, reset, confirmation, and second-take evidence.; Certify: require knowledge, independent performance, and consistency; trainers also require transfer proof.; Audit: recheck on another shift, under pressure, and ideally with another qualified observer.
Demonstration passes: Normal speed -> Watch the complete flow and identify what stands out; Slow narration -> Ask questions and name decisions/checkpoints; Normal speed again -> Predict the next decision while the trainer works at service pace
