  ('search-cur-trainer-shift-autonomy', 'cur-trainer-shift-autonomy', 'module', 'Training Shifts + the Independence Ladder', 'Schedule training as development, not disguised labor, and transfer ownership in safe stages.
Outcomes: Plan one priority behavior for the shift; Assign a safe independence level; Hand off evidence and the next exact rep
Manager protection rule: Do not assign a trainer a normal full workload and expect a complete learning experience on top of it. Schedule the responsibility, name the objective, and protect enough bandwidth to observe.
Independence ladder: Introduced - learner has seen and discussed the standard; Rehearsed - controlled reps completed with coaching; Live with direction - trainer provides active cues; Live with check - learner acts, trainer verifies checkpoints; Independent certification rep - no coaching unless safety requires intervention; Certified - evidence meets the role standard; Audited - behavior survives another shift and observer
Every training shift: Review prior evidence; Name one priority objective; Confirm current source and materials; State ownership and stop points; Create base rep, second take, and variation; Use Keep / Start / Stop; Document status, evidence, risk, exact next rep, and manager handoff
